WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 6: People and Work.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.600
Welcome to Unit 6!

3
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.660
In this unit the focus is on people and work.

4
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.240
You will explore the many different jobs and
professions that keep communities running,

5
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.020
from physicians and lawyers to food vendors and commentators.

6
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.100
You will learn how people choose their
careers, what skills different jobs require,

7
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:29.000
and how the world of work connects to ideas of
fairness, justice, and community responsibility.

8
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:34.820
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:42.080
By the end of this unit, you will be able to identify
and describe a range of professions and career paths,

10
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.200
explaining the skills and training each one requires.

11
00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.700
you will also explain how personal interests
and strengths can guide career choices.

12
00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:57.600
you will also read a passage about careers and jobs and
answer comprehension questions at different thinking levels.

13
00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.540
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:07.840
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: wisdom,
script, text, commentary, observation, caption.

15
00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:13.320
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.520
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:25.760
The reading sequence includes People and Work:
source text 1 and People and Work: source text 2.

18
00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:27.260
Read actively.

19
00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:31.800
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:35.560
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:39.460
The first language focus is What Are Compound Nouns?.

22
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:47.520
A compound noun is a noun made up of two or more words that
come together to create a new word with a specific meaning.

23
00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:54.840
Understanding compound nouns is important because
they help us express complex ideas in a simple way.

24
00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:01.020
For example, instead of saying “the fees
for tuition,” we can say tuition fees.

25
00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:05.380
Instead of saying “the room where the
court meets,” we can say courtroom.

26
00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.520
Compound nouns make our language
clearer, more precise, and more efficient.

27
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.940
Why Do Compound Nouns Matter?

28
00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:20.380
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

29
00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:25.293
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Career Interview Role-Play.

30
00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:30.340
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

31
00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.120
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

32
00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.740
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

33
00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.440
You are ready to begin.

34
00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:45.740
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

35
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.340
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

36
00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:53.980
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
